  "raw_response": "```python\ndef solve(grid):\n    from collections import Counter\n\n    if not grid:\n        return []\n    H = len(grid)\n    W = len(grid[0])\n\n    # Identify the two background colors (most frequent)\n    flat = [v for row in grid for v in row]\n    cnt = Counter(flat)\n    bg_colors = [c for c, _ in cnt.most_common(2)]\n    bg_set = set(bg_colors)\n\n    # Determine base color for every cell.\n    # For background cells, base is their own color.\n    # For markers, infer from neighboring background cells.\n    base_grid = [[0] * W for _ in range(H)]\n    markers = []  # list of (r, c, color)\n\n    for r in range(H):\n        for c in range(W):\n            val = grid[r][c]\n            if val in bg_set:\n                base_grid[r][c] = val\n            else:\n                markers.append((r, c, val))\n                neigh = []\n                for dr in (-1, 0, 1):\n                    for dc in (-1, 0, 1):\n                        if dr == 0 and dc == 0:\n                            continue\n                        nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc\n                        if 0 <= nr < H and 0 <= nc < W:\n                            nv = grid[nr][nc]\n                            if nv in bg_set:\n                                neigh.append(nv)\n                # Choose the most common neighboring background color\n                if neigh:\n                    base_grid[r][c] = Counter(neigh).most_common(1)[0][0]\n                else:\n                    base_grid[r][c] = bg_colors[0]\n\n    # Build mapping: background color -> marker color\n    mapping = {}\n    for r, c, mcolor in markers:\n        b = base_grid[r][c]\n        mapping[b] = mcolor\n\n    # Prepare output as copy of input\n    out = [row[:] for row in grid]\n\n    # Emit diagonal rays from each marker\n    dirs = [(-1, -1), (-1, 1), (1, -1), (1, 1)]\n    for r, c, _ in markers:\n        for dr, dc in dirs:\n            nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc\n            while 0 <= nr < H and 0 <= nc < W:\n                b = base_grid[nr][nc]\n                if b in mapping:\n                    out[nr][nc] = mapping[b]\n                nr += dr\n                nc += dc\n\n    return out\n```",
  "script": "def solve(grid):\n    from collections import Counter\n\n    if not grid:\n        return []\n    H = len(grid)\n    W = len(grid[0])\n\n    # Identify the two background colors (most frequent)\n    flat = [v for row in grid for v in row]\n    cnt = Counter(flat)\n    bg_colors = [c for c, _ in cnt.most_common(2)]\n    bg_set = set(bg_colors)\n\n    # Determine base color for every cell.\n    # For background cells, base is their own color.\n    # For markers, infer from neighboring background cells.\n    base_grid = [[0] * W for _ in range(H)]\n    markers = []  # list of (r, c, color)\n\n    for r in range(H):\n        for c in range(W):\n            val = grid[r][c]\n            if val in bg_set:\n                base_grid[r][c] = val\n            else:\n                markers.append((r, c, val))\n                neigh = []\n                for dr in (-1, 0, 1):\n                    for dc in (-1, 0, 1):\n                        if dr == 0 and dc == 0:\n                            continue\n                        nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc\n                        if 0 <= nr < H and 0 <= nc < W:\n                            nv = grid[nr][nc]\n                            if nv in bg_set:\n                                neigh.append(nv)\n                # Choose the most common neighboring background color\n                if neigh:\n                    base_grid[r][c] = Counter(neigh).most_common(1)[0][0]\n                else:\n                    base_grid[r][c] = bg_colors[0]\n\n    # Build mapping: background color -> marker color\n    mapping = {}\n    for r, c, mcolor in markers:\n        b = base_grid[r][c]\n        mapping[b] = mcolor\n\n    # Prepare output as copy of input\n    out = [row[:] for row in grid]\n\n    # Emit diagonal rays from each marker\n    dirs = [(-1, -1), (-1, 1), (1, -1), (1, 1)]\n    for r, c, _ in markers:\n        for dr, dc in dirs:\n            nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc\n            while 0 <= nr < H and 0 <= nc < W:\n                b = base_grid[nr][nc]\n                if b in mapping:\n                    out[nr][nc] = mapping[b]\n                nr += dr\n                nc += dc\n\n    return out",
